  "text": "Mealie\nLogout\nChange Me\nFavorite Recipes\nCreate\nRecipes\nRecipe Finder\nMeal Planner\nShopping Lists\nTimeline\nCookbooks\nOrganizers\n1\nAnnouncements\nSettings\nMeal Plan Rules\nYou can create rules for auto selecting recipes for your meal plans. These rules are used by the server to determine the random pool of recipes to select from when creating meal plans. Note that if rules have the same day/type constraints then the rule filters will be merged. In practice, it's unnecessary to create duplicate rules, but it's possible to do so.\nNew Rule\nWhen creating a new rule for a meal plan you can restrict the rule to be applicable for a specific day of the week and/or a specific type of meal. To apply a rule to all days or all meal types you can set the rule to \"Any\" which will apply it to all the possible values for the day and/or meal type.\nRule Day\nAny\nMeal Type\nAny\nCategories\nis one of\nShow Advanced\nAdd Field\nThis rule will apply to all days for all meal types.\nCreate\nRecipe Rules\nApplies on fridays for dinner meal types\nCategories\nis one of\nDinner",
  "text_truncated": false,
  "title": "Meal Plan Settings",
